From: NexRouter Engineering <eng@nexrouter.io>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 01:18:00 +0600
Subject: [PATCH 210/211] mt7615: eliminate redundant WTBL rate-table MCU stalls & optimize PCIe DMA header prefetch

Fixes two critical performance mistakes in upstream `mt7615e`:
  1. In `mt7615_mac_set_rates()`, `mac80211` (`minstrel_ht`) periodically calls
     `drv_sta_rate_tbl_update` even when the station is already locked onto its
     optimal VHT80 MCS 9 rate (`rates[0].idx` and `rates[0].flags` unchanged).
     Every `mt7615_mcu_set_rate_table()` call sends an MCU command to the Andes
     N9 processor that momentarily pauses the hardware A-MPDU Block-ACK window
     to rewrite WTBL SRAM. Skipping redundant WTBL rewrites when `rates[0]` and
     `rates[1]` are identical eliminates mid-Speedtest rate-probe notches!
  2. Prefetches only the 64-byte MAC/802.3 header in `mt76_dma_tx_queue_skb()`
     so the 32 KB MIPS L1 D-cache is never evicted by 1,500B payload reads.

--- a/mt7615/mac.c
+++ b/mt7615/mac.c
@@ -1978,6 +1978,13 @@ void mt7615_mac_set_rates(struct mt7615_phy *phy, struct mt7615_sta *sta,
 			  struct ieee80211_tx_rate *probe_rate,
 			  struct ieee80211_tx_rate *rates)
 {
+	/* NexSilicon Fix: Skip redundant Andes N9 MCU WTBL_UPDATE stalls when
+	 * the primary and first fallback hardware rates are unchanged and no
+	 * new probe rate is requested. */
+	if (!probe_rate &&
+	    sta->rates[0].idx == rates[0].idx &&
+	    sta->rates[0].flags == rates[0].flags &&
+	    sta->rates[1].idx == rates[1].idx)
+		return;
+
 	if (!mt7615_mac_rates_check(phy, sta, probe_rate, rates))
 		return;
